# The shipped TLS terminator for the OTLP traces path.
#
# The engine refuses cleartext http to any non-loopback host — no override
# exists — and since round-four #8 that rule finally reaches the OTLP
# exporter too, which had been an unpoliced second HTTP client with no TLS
# backend linked at all. `tempo` is a compose-network host, not loopback, so
# the hop runs through this terminator.
#
# Caddy's internal CA issues the certificate; the CA root lands on the
# `tempo-tls-data` volume at
# /data/caddy/pki/authorities/local/root.crt, which the engine mounts
# read-only and PINS via UNDERCROFT_OTLP_CA. A declared pin REPLACES the
# public roots — that is the point of pinning an internal CA.
#
# The same shape works in production: any TLS front (Caddy, nginx, HAProxy)
# plus a declared root. This mirrors deploy/embeddings-tls/ exactly, which is
# the precedent it was modelled on.
{
	auto_https disable_redirects
}

https://tempo-tls {
	tls internal
	reverse_proxy tempo:4318
}
